            <ArticleTitle>Opportunities to improve pain management outcomes in total knee replacements: patient-centered care across the continuum.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>4-9; quiz 10-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/NOR.0000000000000109</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Despite the importance of pain management to each patient's overall experience with a total knee replacement, opportunities to improve pain care exist. The authors target an unnecessarily fragmented pain management trajectory as one cause of variability in pain outcomes. They propose that a technology-enhanced patient-centered pain management continuum running from the preoperative through the recovery phase offers effective and efficient pain management.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
